Vita, measurement only (--vita-fast-draw-runs=on): what ends the look ahead of each draw run.
The console session of 13 Nov and Vita3K agree that a run holds 16 quads on average in the Palace of
Twilight although the limit is 255, and publishing the squares to the worker together (tried
on 13 Nov, removed) does not change it, so something in the stream ends the runs. Counted for runs and for draws that stayed alone:
the end of the published bytes, a BP write that changes a value, an XF write, a CP write,
another draw command, any other command, the vertex limit, an indexed vertex descriptor; and
the runs by size. Reported with the draw-runs receipts.

--- a/lib/gx/command_processor.cpp
+++ b/lib/gx/command_processor.cpp
@@ -728,6 +728,12 @@ constexpr u32 RunMaxVtxSize = 64;
 u8 sRunBuf[RunVertexLimit * RunMaxVtxSize];
 int sRunMode = -1;         // -1 not read yet, 0 off, 1 on, 2 verify
 u32 sRunCounts[4];         // runs, draws joined, verify candidates, verify mismatches
+// patches/aurora/0027 (measurement only): what ended each look ahead, for runs ([0]) and for
+// draws that stayed alone ([1]): 0 the published bytes ended, 1 a BP write that changes a value,
+// 2 an XF write, 3 a CP write, 4 another draw command, 5 any other command or a draw this one
+// cannot take, 6 the vertex limit, 7 a vertex descriptor with indexed attributes.
+u32 sRunEnds[2][8];
+u32 sRunSizes[2][4];       // quads ([0]) and triangles ([1]) per run: 2-4, 5-16, 17-64, more
 const u8* sRunExpect = nullptr; // verify: where the next joining draw command starts
 
 inline int draw_runs_mode() noexcept {
@@ -755,6 +761,13 @@ extern "C" int twv_gx_fast_draw_runs_stats(uint32_t* counts, unsigned n) noexcep
   return sRunMode < 0 ? 0 : sRunMode;
 }
 
+// patches/aurora/0027: the 16 look-ahead end counts, then the 8 run-size counts.
+extern "C" void twv_gx_fast_draw_runs_census(uint32_t* counts, unsigned n) noexcept {
+  for (unsigned i = 0; i < n && i < 24; ++i) {
+    counts[i] = i < 16 ? sRunEnds[i / 8][i % 8] : sRunSizes[(i - 16) / 4][(i - 16) % 4];
+  }
+}
